{
  "kind": "projections",
  "$comment": "The projection registry (Phase 503): one row per committed artefact this repository GENERATES, and the only list of them. A row names the file (`path`, repository-relative; `{package}` stands for a package id where the packable roster decides which files exist), the tool's family that writes it (`render`, `dotnet run --project tools/Fuaran.Core.Tools -- render <family>`, Phase 532), the approval switch and filter stem that rewrite it from inside the suite (`switch`, `stem`), the test module whose family reds when it drifts (`heldBy`), the whole-file copies other repositories carry of it (`copies`, each `<repo>:<path>` with both halves relative to the workspace root, the ONE spelling of a copy), the SHARED indexes in other repositories that carry this file's rows beside rows other producers own (`rowIn`, the same spelling; DECISIONS.md D211: such a file is no copy of this one, so it is never a `copies` record — the rows this repository owns are held by its family's corpus-freshness leg, and a file the exporter table's writer merges into may be declared only this way), and whether the version ledger reads it as a derived file stamped with the version (`versionStamped`). A row may carry a render, a switch, both, or neither (a render held by its family and regenerated by hand from the family's failure). Approval.fs reads the stems from here, and the `Projections` family holds the rest: every row's file exists, every family the tool renders and every switch stem the suite has is a row, and the four records restated from this list are its renders, held byte for byte (.fantomasignore names every generated F# row; version-derives.json's `derives` and copies.json's `records` are the rows with copies; CONTRIBUTING.md's switch table is the rows with a switch). A new generated artefact is one row here.",
